# SOC L1 Alert Triage

## Summary
Alert triage is when an alert shows up in the siem or soar and the SOC determines if it is good or bad then L2 looks into the threats. 

## Key Concepts
- Alert - a notification ggenerated by a security solution when a specific event or sequence of eventd occur. 

## Alert managemnt solutions
- SIEM - alert management capabilities
- EDR or NDR - not reccomended, seperate alert dashboard
- SOAR - Bigger SOC teams, centeralize alerts from multiple solutions.
- ITSM - a custom ticket management 

## What are the roles in Alert Triage
- SOC L1 analyst - Review alerts, seperate good and bad, sned bad to L2
- SOC L2 analyst - preform deep analysis and remediation on bad alerts
- SOC engineer - ensure alerts contain info requires for triage
- SOC manager - track speed and quality of triage, accuracy of alerts so threats wont be missed

## Alert Proporties
- Time - time of alert
- Name - summary of what happened
- Severity - low, medium, high, critical
- Status - new, in progress, closed
- verdict - classification, true positive or false positive
- Assignee - analyst assigned to review alert
- Description - three sectiond about the alert
- Fields - analyst comment
